conductor-files-selinux: SELinux policy for the conductor-files agent
=====================================================================

The modules "conductor_files" and "conductor_files_port" (targeted policy,
priority 200) confine /usr/bin/conductor-files (conductor-files.service,
root with the unit's capability set) in conductor_files_t and label its
port.

  conductor_files_conf_t     /etc/conductor-files (agent.toml)
  conductor_files_var_lib_t  /var/lib/conductor-files (key pair, pinned keys, audit log)
  conductor_files_port_t     TCP 7443

The agent manages Samba's registry configuration and databases
(/var/lib/samba), runs net, sharesec, samba-tool, smbstatus, smbcontrol,
wbinfo and testparm in its own domain, and manages folders and ACLs under
the share roots, which must carry Samba's share type:

  semanage fcontext -a -t samba_share_t '/srv/shares(/.*)?'
  restorecon -R /srv/shares

Another agent port:

  semanage port -a -t conductor_files_port_t -p tcp 7444

Troubleshooting:

  ausearch -m AVC,USER_AVC -ts recent -c conductor-files
  semanage permissive -a conductor_files_t     (and -d to revert)

License
-------

The policy sources here (.te, .fc, .if, .cil) are Apache-2.0, like the
rest of the repository. The compiled modules expand macros and interfaces
of the SELinux reference policy shipped by selinux-policy-devel, which is
GPL-2.0-or-later, so the binary package is licensed "Apache-2.0 AND
GPL-2.0-or-later" and carries the reference policy's COPYING in
/usr/share/licenses/<package>/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES. Apache-2.0 alone is
not possible for the compiled modules. The corresponding source is this
repository at the release commit and the Fedora selinux-policy source
package of the version the modules were compiled against.
